## Beat 20: Dominic Murders Federal Agent Jensen

BANG!

Jensen’s eyes go wide. Blood sprays forward onto Franko and Judd.

Jensen crumples forward, revealing DOMINIC in the doorway behind him. Bobby at his shoulder. Dominic lowers his gun with practiced calm.

Silence. Everyone processing.

Dominic steps over Jensen’s body like it’s a puddle on the sidewalk.

FRANKO
Fuck!

JUDD
You fucking killed that guy!

DOMINIC
(not looking at them)
I did.

Jensen’s radio CRACKLES on the floor. A beat of silence. Then—

RANDALL (RADIO)
Jensen. Jensen, respond. Do NOT engage. I’m ten minutes out. Jensen—

The voice keeps calling. No one answers. Dominic glances at the radio, then steps over it.

## Beat 21: Dominic Discovers He Was the Target
INT. STORAGE FACILITY - UNIT 447 - CONTINUOUS #31#

Dominic moves through the unit. Purpose. Scanning files. He pulls documents marked “FACILITY - CLASSIFIED.”

Then he reaches the evidence wall. Stops.

Photos of him. Dozens. His diner booth at Gino’s. His sedan. His face in profile, shot through a long lens. Timestamps and annotations in Sal’s handwriting. Movement logs. Pattern analysis. A timeline that stretches back months.

DOMINIC
(quiet)
That sneaky little bitch.

He traces a finger across the wall. Every meeting. Every route. Every habit — mapped, cataloged, owned by someone else.

FRANKO
(nervous, eyeing the door)
Dom, we really need to—

Dominic doesn’t hear him. His flashlight has found the corner.

Ziploc bags. Gallon-sized, the kind you’d marinate chicken in. Inside each one — a jar. His jars. His collection. Each bag tagged with an evidence number and a description written in clinical federal shorthand.

Dominic picks one up. Holds it under the light. Turns it over. The evidence tag reads: “ITEM 23 - BIOLOGICAL SPECIMEN - MALE GENITALIA (PRESERVED)”

His hands are shaking. We’ve never seen that before.

DOMINIC
These are mine.

He picks up another. And another. Stacking them in his arms.

DOMINIC (CONT’D)
(to no one)
These are all mine.

Bobby, Franko, and Judd watch a crime boss cradle bagged dicks like a man collecting photos from a burning house.

BOBBY
Dom. We gotta go.

Nothing.

BOBBY (CONT’D)
DOM.

Nothing. Dominic’s reading every evidence tag. Every clinical description of something that was sacred to him.

BOBBY (CONT’D)
(grabbing Dominic’s arm)
DOM! NOW! He said ten minutes! That was five minutes ago!

Dominic snaps back. Looks at Bobby. Looks at the bags in his arms. A man choosing between his past and his future.

He shoves as many bags as he can carry into his jacket. Lets the rest fall.

DOMINIC
Grab the manifests. Go.

Franko and Judd scramble to collect files. They move toward the door.

Dominic takes one last look at the wall of his own life, documented by a dead man. Then he follows.

## Beat 22: Corridor Convergence

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - CORRIDOR A - CONTINUOUS #32#

Dominic’s group moves through the corridor. Bobby leading. Franko and Judd behind him with armfuls of files. Dominic last — present but somewhere else.

Their footsteps echo off concrete.

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - ENTRANCE CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS #33#

Randall enters the facility. Alone. Weapon drawn. Moving with the controlled urgency of a man who already knows he’s too late but can’t accept it.

His footsteps echo off concrete.

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - CORRIDOR A - CONTINUOUS #34#

Bobby checks corners. Motions the group forward. They turn left.

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - CORRIDOR B - CONTINUOUS #35#

Randall passes numbered units. His eyes track each one. He turns right.

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - CORRIDOR A - CONTINUOUS #36#

Franko’s breathing is loud. Someone’s shoe squeaks on the polished floor. Bobby shoots a look back. They slow down.

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - CORRIDOR B - CONTINUOUS #37#

Randall slows. Listens. Something ahead. He raises his weapon.

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - CORRIDOR A - CONTINUOUS #38#

Bobby raises a fist. Everyone stops. He listens. Something ahead.

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - MAIN CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS #39#

Both corridors feed into the same hallway.

They round the corner at the same time.

## Beat 23: Randall and Dominic Face Off

Fifty feet of fluorescent-lit concrete between them.

Full stop. No one moves.

Close on RANDALL. His weapon comes up but his body goes still. The blurry surveillance photo on his evidence board — made flesh. Three years of hunting. And here he is.

Close on DOMINIC. He doesn’t know this man’s name. But he reads the badge. The weapon. The eyes. He knows exactly what this is.

A long beat. Just breathing and the hum of overhead lights.

RANDALL
(quiet, almost to himself)
Dominic Santoro.

The way he says it isn’t a command. It’s a man confirming something he’s dreamed about for three years.

Dominic holds the eye contact. Reads something in Randall’s face — the obsession, the grief, the years.

DOMINIC
(just as quiet)
You must be the ass man.

The moment fractures—

Dominic FIRES. The shot echoes like a cannon in the enclosed space. Randall dives behind a support column.

Bobby shoves Franko and Judd toward a side corridor.

BOBBY
GO!

Randall returns fire from cover. Controlled. Two shots.

Dominic ducks behind a row of storage units. The group splits — Bobby leading Franko and Judd toward the exit, Dominic providing cover.

DOMINIC
(to Bobby)
Get them out. I’m right behind you.

Randall moves from column to column, closing the distance.

RANDALL
(calling out)
Three years, Dominic. Three years I’ve been looking for you.

DOMINIC
(from cover)
And now you’ve seen me. Happy?

Bobby spots a fire extinguisher on the wall. Grabs it. DISCHARGES it into the corridor. White chemical fog erupts, swallowing the space.

Visibility drops to zero.

Footsteps. Running. The EXIT door slams open somewhere in the fog.

Silence.

Randall stands alone in the clearing haze. Gun raised at nothing.

EXT. STORAGE FACILITY - PARKING LOT - CONTINUOUS #40#

Engines. Tires SCREECH. They’re gone.

## Beat 24: Randall Finds Jensen

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - MAIN CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS #41#

Randall lowers his weapon. The fog settles around his feet.

He doesn’t pursue. He turns back into the facility. Walking now. Slower.

He follows the corridors back the way they came. Past numbered units. The hum of lights.

He rounds a corner. Sees legs protruding from Unit 447.

INT. STORAGE FACILITY - UNIT 447 - CONTINUOUS #42#

Randall rushes in. Drops to his knees beside Jensen.

Jensen’s eyes are open. Vacant. Already gone.

Randall stays there. A hand on Jensen’s shoulder. The evidence wall behind them — photos of Dominic staring down at a dead agent like spectators at a funeral.

A beat.

A dropped manifest page on the floor near Jensen’s hand. Randall picks it up. Partial coordinates visible: “FACILITY B-7”

He stands. Slow. Deliberate.

RANDALL
(into radio)
Officer down. Storage Facility B. Unit 447.

