**CUT TO BLACK.**

# Act Three
## Beat 25: Edith Arrested While Team Hides at Cabin

**Beat of silence.**

**Sound of eggs sizzling.**

CUT TO:

EXT. DOMINIC’S CABIN - MORNING #43#

A rustic hunting lodge that’s been infected by boutique hotel sensibilities. Solar panels on a moss-covered roof. A Tesla charging station next to a rusted pickup on blocks. The kind of place where millennials would pay $400/night to “disconnect.”

INT. DOMINIC’S CABIN - KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS #44#

Black and white checkered floor like a diner that lost its mind. Taxidermie’d animals frozen in compromising positions. Vintage medical equipment repurposed as fruit bowls. Antique doll heads lined up on shelves, glass eyes witnessing everything.

DOMINIC tends eggs on a stove. Burgundy silk kimono embroidered with shapes that could be dragons or could be medical diagrams.

At the kitchen island, FRANKO and JUDD. Yesterday’s clothes. Yesterday’s blood spatter. Today’s existential crisis.

Silence. Just eggs cooking. A clock ticking somewhere.

Coffee cups sit untouched. Nobody’s hungry.

FRANKO  
So... we just gonna pretend we didn’t kill a fed last night?

DOMINIC  
(quiet, distant)  
We’re having breakfast.

He plates eggs with mechanical precision. Sets them down. Nobody moves to eat.

More silence.

FRANKO  
Hey, where’s ya boy Bobby?

DOMINIC  
He’s been in the bathroom all morning.

Beat.

Dominic stares at his eggs like they might explain how he got here.

DOMINIC (CONT’D)  
They took my collection.

FRANKO  
Collection?

DOMINIC  
My dicks.

JUDD  
What?

DOMINIC  
(flat, matter-of-fact)  
Those jars at the storage unit. They were dicks. Guys’ dicks. In jars.

He pushes eggs around his plate, lost in thought.

In the corner, a TV plays muted morning news. A weatherman points at clouds nobody cares about.

Franko glances at the screen.

FRANKO  
Dude! Look!

He points frantically at the TV. The weather has cut to BREAKING NEWS.

FRANKO (CONT’D)  
Turn it up!

Dominic finds the remote with the weary movements of a man who’s given up on surprises. Clicks.

NEWS ANCHOR (ON TV)  
—arrested this morning in connection with what authorities are calling the “Kiddie Pool Killer” case. The 73-year-old grandmother is accused of dissolving a federal agent in her basement using a combination of household chemicals and—

The anchor pauses, clearly reading ahead.

NEWS ANCHOR (ON TV) (CONT’D)  
(struggling)  
—what investigators describe as “an alarming disregard for proper ventilation.”

Cut to: Shaky cellphone footage. EDITH in full glory—curlers like armor, ratty housecoat like a battle flag—being perp-walked by overwhelmed officers.

EDITH (ON TV)  
THE GOVERNMENT’S BEEN UP MY ASS FOR YEARS! NOW I KNOW WHY!

She breaks free momentarily, pointing directly at the camera.

EDITH (ON TV) (CONT’D)  
CHECK YOUR COLONS, PEOPLE! THEY GOT CAMERAS UP THERE! PROBABLY STREAMING TO PUTIN RIGHT NOW!

An OFFICER tries to guide her toward the squad car.

OFFICER (ON TV)  
Ma’am, please—

EDITH (ON TV)  
DON’T TOUCH ME! I KNOW MY RIGHTS! I WATCH FOX NEWS!

Two more officers join the effort. It takes all three to wrestle her into the vehicle.

EDITH (ON TV) (CONT’D)  
(muffled through squad car window)  
THE BASEMENT SMELLS LIKE MILLENNIAL FAILURE! I NEVER GO DOWN THERE!

Back to the studio. The anchor looks like he needs therapy.

NEWS ANCHOR (ON TV)  
The suspect’s nephew remains at large and is considered—

Dominic clicks off the TV. The sudden silence is deafening.

DOMINIC  
(mild interest)  
I take it you know her?

JUDD  
(hollow)  
I’m the nephew.

Dominic sets down the remote with deliberate care. When he speaks, his voice carries the weight of someone who’s watched systems grow beyond their stated purpose.

DOMINIC  
(quiet, thoughtful)  
They always say it’s just for the bad guys. Just the dealers, the killers. But surveillance is hungry. Today it’s your grandmother. Tomorrow it’s everyone who takes longer than five minutes to shit.

Beat. The absurdity and truth of it hangs in the air.

FRANKO  
What the fuck do we do now? I used to always say Budapest as a joke but like...  
(beat)  
...maybe Budapest?

JUDD  
(shaking his head)  
I don’t know, man. I don’t think I could live with myself with Nans locked up because of me.

The kitchen feels smaller suddenly. Three criminals and their untouched breakfast, processing the reality that they’re well and truly fucked.

Dominic picks up his fork. Sets it down. The eggs have gone cold.

Outside, a bird calls. Normal morning sounds for a deeply abnormal morning.

## Beat 26: Bobby Exposed as FBI Informant with Tracker
INT. DOMINIC’S CABIN - KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS #45#

The untouched breakfast congeals on plates. Franko scrolls his phone with the desperation of a man planning an escape.

FRANKO
Look at this—two bedroom in Budapest, 400 euros a month. Comes with a bidet.

He holds up the phone showing a suspiciously nice apartment.

FRANKO (CONT’D)
