FRANKO (CONT’D)
(to Dominic)
Jesus. I think your plumbing needs a priest dude.

Bobby groans, a sound that suggests his intestines are negotiating a hostile takeover. He shuffles toward the table, each step a victory against gravity.

BOBBY
(barely audible)
Three days... nothing... it’s like concrete in there...

He collapses into a chair. The universe, having a dark sense of humor, has placed him directly next to Sal’s tracker sitting on the table.

The tracker suddenly BEEPS. Its LED flashes green.

Bobby’s eyes go wide.

BOBBY (CONT’D)
Oh fuck, it’s happening—

What follows is a sound that defies description. Part foghorn, part garbage disposal, part soul leaving body. The dam hasn’t just broken—it’s been obliterated.

BOBBY (CONT’D)
JESUS FUCK!

Everyone scrambles back. Chairs scraping. Franko drops his phone.

DOMINIC
(eyes narrowing)
Bobby. Why did you just shit yourself-
-when that *thing* lit up?

Bobby’s struggling. Sweaty, messy, trippin’ balls.

DOMINIC (CONT’D)
You have one of those things don’t you?!

Bobby tries to back away but he’s still... occupied.

DOMINIC (CONT’D)
I always believed you when you said you had IBS. I’m such a fucking idiot! Tell me-
(a beat)
