DOMINIC
Agent Randall.

INT. FACILITY B-7 - LAB 7 DOORWAY - CONTINUOUS #89#

Randall spins from Bobby’s body, hand flying to his holster.

Sees Dominic at the far end of the corridor. Fifty feet of sterile white between them.

RANDALL
Dominic Santoro.
In the flesh.

INT. FACILITY B-7 - SUB-LEVEL 2 CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS #90#

Dominic raises his hands slowly, theatrical.

DOMINIC
I’m unarmed.

Randall steps over Bobby’s legs into the corridor. Controller in one hand, other hovering near his weapon.

He begins his approach. Not rushing. The walk of a man who’s imagined this moment for three years and intends to savor every step. Skyfall energy. A villain who’s already won and wants you to know it.

Twenty feet.

RANDALL
Three years I’ve been hunting you.

Fifteen feet. His footsteps metronomic on the tile.

RANDALL (CONT’D)
You know how I found your people, Dominic? Not wiretaps. Not informants ratting you out over coffee.

Ten feet. Close enough to see the sweat on Dominic’s temple.

RANDALL (CONT’D)
I found them from the inside.

He stops. Face to face. Studies Dominic the way a collector studies an acquisition.

RANDALL (CONT’D)
I know when your men are scared. Not because they tell me — because their bodies tell me. Cortisol spikes. Heart rate. Sphincter tension.
(a beat)
The body doesn’t know how to lie, Dominic.

Randall begins to circle him. Slow. Intimate. The way Dominic circled Sal in that cottage. The same predatory geometry.

RANDALL (CONT’D)
(behind him now, close enough that his breath hits Dominic’s neck)
I’ve been inside forty-seven of your associates. I know their rhythms. When they sleep. When they’re anxious. When they’ve eaten something that disagrees with them.

He places a hand on Dominic’s shoulder. Dominic doesn’t flinch, but something shifts in his eyes.

RANDALL (CONT’D)
(almost tender)
I know them more intimately than their wives do. More intimately than their mothers did. I possess the most private part of who they are.

He circles back around to face Dominic. Closer now. Intimate distance.

RANDALL (CONT’D)
And they never even knew.

Something is happening on Dominic’s face. Not rage. Not shame. Recognition. Horrible, dawning recognition.

RANDALL (CONT’D)
That’s real power. Not killing a man. Anyone can kill a man.
(a beat)
Owning a piece of him he doesn’t even know you have.

The words land like a mirror held up to a face that doesn’t want to see itself. Dominic’s hands, still raised, are trembling. Not from fear.

He sees it now. The collection. The jars. Forty-seven pieces of men who never consented to being possessed. Trophies of intimacy taken by force. He and Randall — the same sickness, different instruments.

Randall reads the tremor. Misreads it as weakness. Leans in, voice dropping to a whisper.

RANDALL (CONT’D)
The beautiful thing about my program? It’s honest. No pretense. Just pure, unfiltered access to a man’s deepest...

He reaches around Dominic like he’s going to pat him down. The controller brushes against Dominic’s hip.

RANDALL (CONT’D)
...self.

BEEP.

Electronic. Sharp. Wrong.

Randall freezes. Pulls back. Checks his controller.

The screen shows: “DEVICE DETECTED - SYNCING...”

Confusion flickers across his face.

Dominic’s trembling stops. His eyes are clear. Whatever just broke inside him has settled into something harder. Quieter.

DOMINIC
Tell me, Randall.

He reaches into his pocket. Slow. Deliberate.

DOMINIC (CONT’D)
Have you ever been fucked?

